      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you think I haven\u0027t tried?\n\n`IS_ENABLED()` is not a magical tool which will fix everything. In some cases it does more harm than benefits.\n\nIn this case there are two problems\n\nFirst problem is that `struct rollback_data` has `secret` member [only when `CONFIG_ROLLBACK_SECRET_SIZE` is defined](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/rollback_private.h;l\u003d24-26;drc\u003d71b2ef709dcb14260f5fdaa3ab4ced005a29fb46). Of course, if `IS_ENABLED()` is used properly then no access to `secret` will happen, but before these accesses are optimized out the compiler during parsing the code will complain that `secret` is not defined.\n\nSecond problem. When I try to use it I got the following error\n```\nld.lld: error: undefined symbol: IS_ENABLED_BAD_ARGS\n\u003e\u003e\u003e referenced by rollback.c:276 (/home/patryk/chromiumos/src/platform/ec/common/rollback.c:276)\n\u003e\u003e\u003e               build/bloonchipper/RO/common/rollback.o:(rollback_update)\nclang-16: error: ld.lld command failed with exit code 1 (use -v to see invocation)\n```\n\nCould you help me with these issues?",
